# Docker build ignore rules for the api/ build context
# (`docker build -f api/Dockerfile api/`).
#
# NOTE: this file does NOT apply to the repo-root context, which the web image
# uses (`docker build -f web/Dockerfile .`) and which must keep api/ test files:
# `npm run build` runs the unit tests first, and
# web/src/lib/langPlacement.test.ts reads ../../../api/internal/mcpsrv/
# mcp_parity_test.go at image-build time. The root .dockerignore therefore
# excludes no _test.go, on purpose.

# Local Go build output (~60 MB); the image builds its own binary.
bin/

# Test files are not inputs to this build. api/Dockerfile runs `go mod download`
# and `go build ./cmd/jomform-api` only; neither reads a _test.go. Nothing under
# api/scripts/ (the biteproof harnesses, which do name _test.go files) is invoked
# by the build — they run on the host against the checkout — and the runtime
# stage copies just the binary, so no test file is needed at any stage.
#
# WHY `**`, MEASURED NOT ASSUMED (Docker 29.7.1 / buildx 0.36.1, BuildKit):
# a bare pattern in .dockerignore matches the context ROOT only — `*` never
# crosses `/`, exactly as in Go's filepath.Match — so `*_test.go` excluded the
# zero top-level test files and left all 413 nested ones in the context
# (probe: `find /ctx -name '*_test.go' | wc -l` = 413; a scratch context with
# root_test.go + sub/x_test.go and the bare rule kept 1 file). Docker documents
# `**` as matching "any number of directories (including zero)"
# (docs.docker.com/build/concepts/context/#syntax), and the same probe over
# this tree returns 0 with `**/*_test.go`.
#
# Both forms are kept: `**/*_test.go` is what the documented matcher honours,
# and the bare `*_test.go` is the root-level rule that holds under a narrower
# glob implementation, so the exclusion does not depend on one engine's reading
# of `**`. The whole defect was a pattern that looked sufficient and was not.
*_test.go
**/*_test.go
